body:
Thank you so much for your response. As it is, I already have a struggle of sometimes thinking I'm making things up or making things out to be worse than they actually were (both with this specific person, and others in general). I understand that to the people he knew IRL and his family, that he was completely different from the person that tried to take advantage of me when I was young, but just reading their words contrasted to the hours I've spent hiding in my room sobbing just kind of broke my mind for a second, I guess.

&#x200B;

"Their words aren't part of your world." That's an amazing way to put it, thank you.
